WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:17.463
Everyone in the school auditorium was quiet.

2
00:00:17.464 --> 00:00:21.609
We were waiting for Mr. Bright to call out the name of the winner.

3
00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:28.823
"And the winner is Evan Demarco for his Automatic Fish-Feeder!" cried Mr. Bright.

4
00:00:28.824 --> 00:00:32.912
Evan stood up, and everyone clapped and cheered.

5
00:00:32.913 --> 00:00:36.301
I clapped too, but I was stunned.

6
00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:40.032
I felt like a balloon with all the air let out.

7
00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:43.420
I was Iggy the Incredible Inventor.

8
00:00:43.421 --> 00:00:45.278
But I had not won!

9
00:00:45.279 --> 00:00:50.089
Neither of my inventions would be in The Kids' Invention Guide.

10
00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:54.831
I could understand Mr. Bright not choosing the Fabulous Glasses-Finder.

11
00:00:54.832 --> 00:00:57.575
But what about my Pick-a-Number?

12
00:00:57.576 --> 00:01:05.853
All the kids had loved that invention!

13
00:01:05.854 --> 00:01:10.874
On the way out of the assembly, Evan came up to me.

14
00:01:10.875 --> 00:01:13.852
"Thanks, Iggy!" he said.

15
00:01:13.853 --> 00:01:16.737
"For what?" I asked.

16
00:01:16.738 --> 00:01:20.869
"For inspiring me to invent something," said Evan.

17
00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:23.065
I looked at him.

18
00:01:23.066 --> 00:01:25.024
"What do you mean?"

19
00:01:25.025 --> 00:01:29.207
"You always invent such cool things," he said.

20
00:01:29.208 --> 00:01:32.316
"So I wanted to invent something cool too."

21
00:01:32.317 --> 00:01:35.365
"Oh," I answered with a smile.

22
00:01:35.366 --> 00:01:38.323
"Well, congratulations for winning.

23
00:01:38.324 --> 00:01:42.612
Your Automatic Fish-Feeder is a great idea."

24
00:01:42.613 --> 00:01:46.092
I felt better, knowing I had inspired Evan.

25
00:01:46.093 --> 00:01:50.430
But I still couldn't help feeling a little disappointed.

26
00:01:50.431 --> 00:01:55.336
After school Jenny, Josh, Molly, and I went to the park.

27
00:01:55.337 --> 00:02:02.115
"My teacher said I can take my math and spelling tests again," Jenny told us happily.

28
00:02:02.116 --> 00:02:06.983
"And I can see all the way across the park now."

29
00:02:06.984 --> 00:02:10.074
A second later Jenny gasped.

30
00:02:10.075 --> 00:02:13.511
"Look! It's Mr. Bright!"

31
00:02:13.512 --> 00:02:19.150
Sure enough, there was Mr. Bright on the other side of the park.

32
00:02:19.151 --> 00:02:26.802
"He's with a girl on a bike," said Josh.

33
00:02:26.803 --> 00:02:30.706
In a few minutes, we had reached Mr. Bright.

34
00:02:30.707 --> 00:02:33.733
"Hi, Mr. Bright!" said Molly.

35
00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:36.733
"We saw you at our school today."

36
00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:41.008
"You were a great audience," said Mr. Bright.

37
00:02:41.009 --> 00:02:43.504
He turned to the girl on the bike.

38
00:02:43.505 --> 00:02:46.289
"This is my daughter, Emily."

39
00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:49.223
"Hi," said Emily.

40
00:02:49.224 --> 00:02:53.615
"I'm glad to see you kids again," said Mr. Bright.

41
00:02:53.616 --> 00:02:57.097
"There was someone I wanted to talk to at your school today.

42
00:02:57.098 --> 00:03:01.373
He wrote about a really great invention, but I can't remember his name."

43
00:03:01.374 --> 00:03:05.506
"What was the invention?" asked Josh.

44
00:03:05.507 --> 00:03:10.270
"It was called the Fabulous Glasses-Finder," said Mr. Bright.

45
00:03:10.271 --> 00:03:12.308
I couldn't believe it.

46
00:03:12.309 --> 00:03:16.318
"That was my invention!" I cried.

47
00:03:16.319 --> 00:03:20.482
"It's a very interesting idea," said Mr. Bright.

48
00:03:20.483 --> 00:03:25.336
"The only problem is that your glasses-finder is not easy to use."

49
00:03:25.337 --> 00:03:27.698
My heart sank.

50
00:03:27.699 --> 00:03:36.005
"However," said Mr. Bright, "the invention works well for objects bigger than glasses, like bicycles!"

51
00:03:36.005 --> 00:03:40.698
I smiled. "Really?"

52
00:03:40.699 --> 00:03:46.152
"Yes," said Mr. Bright. "Tell them, Emily."

53
00:03:46.153 --> 00:03:50.173
"I ride my bike to school every day," she said.

54
00:03:50.174 --> 00:03:52.235
"Most kids at my school do.

55
00:03:52.236 --> 00:03:56.679
Sometimes there are so many bikes in the racks, it's hard to find yours.

56
00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:00.064
So I put a flower on my handlebars.

57
00:04:00.065 --> 00:04:04.854
And now I can spot my bike right away!"

58
00:04:04.855 --> 00:04:08.892
"It's a brilliant idea!" said Mr. Bright.

59
00:04:08.893 --> 00:04:12.679
I smiled, but something was bothering me.

60
00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:17.652
"But I didn't actually invent a bicycle-finder," I said.

61
00:04:17.653 --> 00:04:21.353
"Of course you did," said Mr. Bright.

62
00:04:21.354 --> 00:04:26.682
"Sometimes a person invents something, and someone else finds another use for it.

63
00:04:26.683 --> 00:04:29.830
That's part of solving problems."

64
00:04:29.831 --> 00:04:33.189
I thought about the number machine at the bakery.

65
00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:37.307
That invention had given me the idea for the Pick-a-Number.

66
00:04:37.308 --> 00:04:43.082
"Be sure to write about another invention next time I visit your school," said Mr. Bright.

67
00:04:43.083 --> 00:04:47.386
"Okay," I said. I grinned happily.

68
00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:51.218
I had solved a problem on the playground.

69
00:04:51.219 --> 00:04:55.093
I had figured out why Jenny was having trouble in school.

70
00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:57.873
I had inspired Evan.

71
00:04:57.874 --> 00:05:03.948
And now, with Mr. Bright's help, I had invented a bicycle-finder.

72
00:05:03.949 --> 00:05:07.461
I, Iggy, hadn't won the contest at school.

73
00:05:07.462 --> 00:05:15.343
But I was still an incredible inventor!
